# Project Rules (summary)

This is a quick reference. Full rules: `AI_RULES.md` (the single source of truth).

## Folder boundaries

- `app/components/` → UI rendering (Nuxt auto-imported)
- `app/composables/` → shared Vue state and UI logic (Nuxt auto-imported)
- `app/pages/` → routes (Nuxt auto-imported)
- `app/layouts/` → page layouts (Nuxt auto-imported)
- `app/components/ui/` → shadcn-vue components (managed via CLI)
- `app/lib/utils.ts` → shadcn-vue `cn()` utility
- `app/assets/css/` → stylesheets, theme CSS variables
- `app/notes/` → pure note domain logic (explicit imports)
- `app/storage/` → persistence (explicit imports)
- `app/config/` → configuration loading (explicit imports)

These folders are approved — create them when first needed.
Do not create folders outside this list (no `utils/`, `helpers/`, `shared/`, or `index.ts` barrel files).

## Conventions

- Components: `PascalCase.vue`
- Composables: `useXxx.ts`
- Domain/storage: `camelCase.ts`
- Tests: `*.test.ts`
- Cross-folder imports: use `~/` alias (e.g. `~/notes/types`)
- Same-folder imports: use relative `./` (e.g. `./types`)

## Quality checks

Run after every change:

- `npm run lint:fix` — ESLint auto-fix
- `npm run format` — Prettier formatting
- `npm run typecheck` — type-check with nuxt typecheck
- `npm run test:unit:ci` — unit tests (Vitest)

Git hooks enforce lint, format, typecheck, unit tests, and conventional commit messages on commit.
Allowed commit prefixes: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `style:`, `build:`, `ci:`, `perf:`.

## Key constraints

- Pure domain logic (`notes/`, `storage/`, `config/`) must not import from Vue.
- Theming uses CSS custom properties via Tailwind/shadcn-vue. No JS token objects.
- Prefer modifying existing files over creating new ones.
- Keep functions small and direct.
- Log decisions in `docs/decisions.md`.
